 flora ” by Krishtofovich (1946), widespread in the temperate zone of the Holarctic including South Siberia in Pliocene (Kuminova, 1960, Ogureeva, 1980). Two species S. mariannae and S. adelaidae are known from Khamar-Daban Ridge in Baikal Region (Buryatia and Irkutskaya Oblast). Two species distributed in West Sayan Mountains: S. ergaki and S. mikhaili Two species are known from Gornaya Shoria mountain massif (Kemerovo Region): S. mikhaili and S. shoricus. A map of the distribution of Sayanazercon in different regions of South Siberia is presented in Fig. 62. Photos of localities in different regions of South Siberia mountains are shown in Figures 63 – 70.","","text","",""]]},"V9KQ2":{"d":[["Distribution. China (Yunnan, Fujian), India, Laos, Thailand, Vietnam.","","text","",""]]},"X89T":{"d":[["Atlantic Ocean","1902","mrgid","",""],["European waters (ERMS scope)","7130","mrgid","",""]]},"YH6F":{"d":[["South Carolina","14632","mrgid","",""],["South Carolina","14632","mrgid","",""]]},"YW85":{"d":[["Australia","","text","",""]]},"YZPZ":{"d":[["","ECU","tdwg","",""]]},"YZQ9":{"d":[["","ECU","tdwg","",""]]},"Z5XV":{"d":[["Rep. South Africa","","text","native",""]]},"Z685":{"d":[["Italy","2133","mrgid","",""]]}}